text:
{
  "summary": "Fashion designer Charlotte Ronson gave Domaine Home a look inside her airy, comfortable New York City apartment. White walls showcase eclectic art, while bright furniture and fresh flowers add colorful accents."
}

{
  "summary": "Although the author considers the Galaxy S7 a superior phone in design, features, and Android experience, its battery repeatedly ran out by early evening under heavy use. They switched to the iPhone 6s Plus because its better software-hardware optimization keeps it running much longer, despite its less appealing design and smaller battery."
}

{
  "summary": "Amy Cazin built Primal Pit Paste, a natural deodorant company, from a $100 investment after making products for her family; it generated more than $800,000 in sales in its first 18 months. She declined an early Walmart offer because the business wasn’t ready to meet the retailer’s volumes, later expanding to Whole Foods and thousands of independent retailers."
}

{
  "summary": "Apps such as iAmAMan and uPMS encourage men to track women colleagues’ and partners’ menstrual cycles, ostensibly to avoid PMS-related conflict. The practice has drawn criticism as intrusive and sexist, particularly after one woman said coworkers began tracking her cycle following a workplace argument."
}

{
  "summary": "A Roomba spreading dog waste illustrates why home robots and smart appliances often disappoint: they can get stuck, cause damage, and require enough supervision and cleanup to limit the time they save. Unlike dishwashers and washing machines, these devices must operate in unpredictable homes, making it difficult for software and robotics to deliver enough practical value to become widely adopted."
}

{
  "summary": "Whole Foods co-CEO Walter Robb says he avoids hiring candidates who lack humility or overemphasize self-promotion. Other employers, including Google, value confident people who can also listen and change their minds; interview experts recommend highlighting collaborators’ contributions and how you’ll help the organization succeed."
}

{
  "summary": "Harvard’s decades-long Grant Study found that people with close, supportive relationships tend to be happier, healthier, and live longer, while loneliness is linked to earlier declines in health and brain function. Research leader Robert Waldinger says nurturing lasting connections matters more than wealth, fame, or career success—and requires ongoing effort."
}

{
  "summary": "Leann surprised her grandfather Ried with an ultrasound photo revealing she was expecting twins, and his emotional reaction grew even bigger when he realized there were two babies. She gave birth to twin girls in February 2016."
}

{
  "summary": "The U.S. is the world’s largest arms exporter, with Saudi Arabia and the United Arab Emirates its biggest recipients from 2011 to 2015; Middle Eastern and Asian demand is driven by regional insecurity and tensions. The article also describes U.S. military financing, rising arms exports from China, and Vietnam’s new eligibility to buy U.S. weapons after the embargo was lifted."
}

{
  "summary": "LendLease sold all 391 apartments in the final stage of its Darling Square development in Sydney within four hours, with prices ranging from A$630,000 to A$3.5 million. The sellout signals resilient demand despite a large pipeline of new apartments due for completion over the next two years."
}

{
  "summary": "BBC golf commentator Peter Alliss was caught on a hot mic at the Masters making remarks about winner Sergio Garcia’s fiancée, Angela Akins, calling her skirt the country’s shortest and joking about the couple’s hotel night. The BBC called the skirt comment inappropriate; the incident renewed criticism of Alliss, whose past remarks about women and golfers have also drawn controversy."
}

{
  "summary": "Drake’s *Views* spent its ninth consecutive week at No. 1 on the Billboard 200, becoming the first album since streaming was added to the chart to sustain such a run with streaming making up a major share of its totals. Its nearly 100 million streams drove most of its latest week’s equivalent sales; another week at No. 1 would tie Adele’s *21* for 10 straight weeks."
}

{
  "summary": "The article compiles alleged warnings from former fast-food and concession workers about items they say may be stale, poorly maintained, or handled in questionable ways—from McDonald’s nuggets and McCafé drinks to KFC BBQ sandwiches and gas-station Slurpees. The claims are presented as employee anecdotes, not independently verified findings; one example, Chipotle’s quesarito, is criticized only for slowing service during busy periods."
}

{
  "summary": "A 1964 photo shows filmmaker Alfred Hitchcock wearing a Beatles-style mop-top wig, in a look that also resembles Three Stooges comedian Moe Howard. The image, noted by Retronaut, is presented as a playful snapshot from the height of Beatlemania."
}

{
  "summary": "After searching remote villages near Denakanikottai, a reporter finds Eranna, a 60-year-old farmer and the last rat catcher in the area. He describes the traditional methods and field rats he hunted for farmers and food, but says he does not plan to pass on the skill, which is likely to disappear as younger generations move to city jobs."
}

{
  "summary": "The author argues that many home-based, often mother-led businesses promoted on social media are legitimate multilevel marketing ventures, not illegal pyramid schemes, and can offer families income and flexibility. She emphasizes the work involved and urges readers to consider supporting small business owners, though the article presents a strongly positive view of MLMs."
}

{
  "summary": "Turing Robotic Industries unveiled the concept for the Turing Phone Cadenza, a proposed superphone running the company’s Swordfish OS with deep-learning AI. Its advertised specs include dual Snapdragon 830 processors, 12GB of RAM, up to 1.5TB of storage, a 60MP camera, support for four SIM cards, and a hybrid battery; the phone was expected to launch the following year."
}

{
  "summary": "A camera seen in footage of a 1995 Mike Tyson fight isn’t evidence of a time traveler: compact digital cameras were already available then. The article says modern viewers can misread old footage through present-day assumptions, as with a 1922 “wireless phone” that was actually a radio."
}

{
  "summary": "Researchers identify Tamu Massif, submerged in the Pacific’s Shatsky Rise, as Earth’s largest volcano: about 400 miles wide and formed by lava flows roughly 144 million years ago. Its size and evidence of a central volcanic cone may help scientists explain how oceanic plateaus form, though its summit remains nearly 2,000 meters below the sea surface."
}

{
  "summary": "Cats may purr to show contentment, communicate hunger, soothe themselves during stress, or even support healing; the sound’s 25–150 Hz frequency overlaps with ranges associated with bone and muscle repair. Scientists still disagree about its purpose, and a purr doesn’t necessarily mean a cat is happy."
}

{
  "summary": "Legendary Simpsons writer John Swartzwelder joined Twitter by posting witty quotes from his detective novels to promote them, rather than writing original jokes. The article playfully suggests this deadpan self-promotion may itself be a brilliant form of comedy."
}

{
  "summary": "Speedrunner BubblesDelFuego beat Fallout 4 in just over an hour by using exploits such as clipping through walls, teleporting across the map, and skipping dialogue, along with a carefully optimized route. The record is a team effort, and the runners believe further discoveries could cut the time to 45–55 minutes."
}

{
  "summary": "The cylinder on many laptop charger cords is a ferrite bead, which reduces high-frequency electromagnetic interference. It helps prevent the cable from transmitting or picking up unwanted radio signals that could disrupt nearby electronics."
}

{
  "summary": "Former truck driver Siphiwe Baleka says poor sleep disrupts hunger and metabolism, contributing to weight gain—especially for truckers whose schedules and sedentary work make restful sleep difficult. He recommends tracking sleep, keeping consistent bed and wake times, avoiding screens before bed, and making the bedroom a place for sleep."
}

{
  "summary": "Houston is projected to overtake Chicago as America’s third-largest city within eight to 10 years, driven by job opportunities, domestic migration, and a growing foreign-born population. Its rapid growth reflects a diverse, increasingly progressive urban Texas, but also brings challenges including traffic, poor air quality, and dependence on the volatile energy industry."
}

{
  "summary": "Studies of hundreds of undergraduates found that women rated men described as skilled storytellers as more attractive for long-term relationships and higher in status, while men did not respond similarly to women storytellers. Researchers suggest storytelling may signal influence or status, but say further research is needed to explain the appeal."
}

{
  "summary": "European menopause guidelines urge employers to account for symptoms that can affect women at work, such as hot flashes, insomnia, and concentration problems. Suggested steps include cooler workspaces, flexible schedules, stress reduction, bathroom access, and manager training, alongside a workplace culture where women feel comfortable discussing symptoms and requesting accommodations."
}

{
  "summary": "The author says meditation is accessible to everyone, has no single correct method, and may improve focus, ease stress, and support health. She introduces a simple one-minute morning meditation learned in China and recommends pairing it with her free guided meditation MP3."
}

{
  "summary": "The article says Bollywood actor and former model Dino Morea has a lookalike in Scott Foley, who plays Jake on the American TV series *Scandal*. It notes that others have noticed their resemblance, pointing readers to a tweet as an example."
}

{
  "summary": "Listeria can contaminate vegetables through soil or animal manure, then persist on food-processing equipment, where it can survive and grow in cold, damp conditions. A recall of Country Fresh precut vegetables followed a positive test, though no illnesses had been reported; the article also outlines food-safety steps, including washing produce and preventing cross-contamination."
}

{
  "summary": "After Slate editor Gabriel Roth criticized Merriam-Webster for being too permissive about language, the dictionary replied, “No one cares how you feel,” prompting widespread praise for its sharp comeback. Merriam-Webster’s editor said the exchange was meant as playful banter and reiterated that dictionaries document how people actually use words, including “mad” to mean “angry.”"
}

{
  "summary": "Kelly Clarkson told Jay Leno that she and husband Brandon Blackstock are actively trying for a baby, joking that they’re “trying ... like rabbits,” while denying she is pregnant. After growing close to Blackstock’s two children, Clarkson said she now hopes to have as many as five kids."
}

{
  "summary": "Romania’s Movile Cave has been isolated from the outside world for about 5.5 million years, creating a dark, toxic environment where scientists have identified 48 species, including 33 found nowhere else. Its ecosystem depends on chemosynthetic bacteria rather than sunlight, and researchers are still investigating how its animals became trapped there and what the cave may reveal about evolution."
}

{
  "summary": "Yogi Adityanath, a Hindu priest and longtime BJP politician, became chief minister of Uttar Pradesh, drawing both fervent support and alarm over his history of anti-Muslim rhetoric and criminal accusations. Though he has struck a more inclusive tone in office, critics warn that he may struggle to rein in hardline supporters as he pursues development and builds his political future."
}

{
  "summary": "Lenovo’s Yoga Book replaces a physical keyboard with a second touch surface that can display a haptic-feedback keyboard or support stylus writing, including digitizing notes written on paper. Its reversible 10.1-inch tablet is under 10mm thick and includes a 1080p display, 4GB of RAM, 64GB of storage, and a microSD slot."
}

{
  "summary": "Marriage therapists urge couples to seek counseling early—ideally before engagement or when problems first emerge—rather than waiting until resentment, defensiveness, or apathy take hold. Therapy can help partners communicate, prepare for future stresses, and stay connected even when some longstanding differences cannot be resolved."
}

{
  "summary": "Apple is reportedly planning to unveil its new iPhones on September 9, though the company has not officially announced the event. The phones may feature Force Touch, an improved camera and a more powerful wireless chip, with new iPads and an Apple TV also potentially on the agenda."
}

{
  "summary": "Shah Rukh Khan said Raees was moved from Sultan’s Eid release to avoid two major films competing for limited theater space, and because Raees still needed some filming. He hoped to release it on January 25 or 26 and said discussions were underway with Hrithik Roshan’s team, since Kaabil was also planned for that period."
}

{
  "summary": "Music psychology research suggests earworms are common but usually not harmful. To disrupt one, try chewing gum, changing your walking pace, singing a different song, socializing, or distracting yourself; prevention may include avoiding repetitive or recent music, especially before bed. Attempts to suppress a song can backfire, so don’t try too hard."
}

{
  "summary": "The white, stringy cords in raw eggs are called chalazae; they anchor the yolk in place and are completely edible. Visible chalazae are also a sign of freshness, as they fade as eggs age."
}

{
  "summary": "Apple warns that the jet-black iPhone 7’s glossy finish may show fine scratches with use and recommends a case for protection. The writer laments that owners may need to cover the attractive finish to keep it pristine, despite the availability of clear cases."
}

{
  "summary": "Michigan Attorney General Bill Schuette argued that the state’s same-sex marriage ban serves its interest in regulating relationships tied to procreation, as a lesbian couple’s constitutional challenge heads toward trial. LGBTQ advocates and families seeking to adopt disputed that reasoning, while polls showed shifting—but conflicting—public opinion on marriage equality in Michigan."
}

{
  "summary": "An unconfirmed report says Avengers: Infinity War will loosely adapt the Infinity Gauntlet comics, with Thanos seeking to impress Death by wiping out half the universe’s life. The Avengers, Guardians of the Galaxy, and Nick Fury are reportedly involved; filming was expected to begin in November ahead of a May 2018 release."
}

{
  "summary": "Thomas Blige, 63, father of singer Mary J. Blige, was reportedly stabbed three times—including in the neck—during a domestic dispute in Battle Creek, Michigan, and was in critical condition after surgery. Police arrested his former girlfriend, who was treated for a cut; the pair had reportedly been involved in multiple domestic violence complaints."
}

{
  "summary": "After nine years of grinding, Tibia player Kharsek became the first to reach level 999 and pass through the game’s long-teased secret door. He then logged off without revealing what was inside; developers also refuse to spoil the secret, while fans speculate that harassment during his quest may explain his silence."
}

{
  "summary": "Recruiter and career coach Tina Nicolai says the most irritating résumé problems she has seen among more than 40,000 submissions are overly long summaries, clichéd jargon, and excessively formal wording. She recommends concise achievement-focused bullets, fresh language, and a more engaging style that conveys personality."
}

{
  "summary": "YouTubers GizmoSlip froze a Galaxy Note 7 in ice for more than 23 hours, then dropped it from 100 feet; the phone emerged unscratched and fully functional. The article contrasts its rugged hardware with reports of software failures and warns readers not to imitate the dangerous stunt."
}

{
  "summary": "Game of Thrones’ seventh season is expected to premiere later than its usual April slot in 2017, though HBO has not announced a date. Showrunners David Benioff and Dan Weiss said filming will start later so they can capture the gloomy weather needed now that winter has arrived in the story."
}

{
  "summary": "Apple unveiled the 12.9-inch iPad Pro at its iPhone 6s event, highlighting its high-resolution display, A9X chip, and claimed 10-hour battery life. In a surprise collaboration, Microsoft employees demonstrated Office on the tablet, which also supports a keyboard cover and side-by-side apps."
}
